Spec: specs/001-core-and-anthropic-passthrough/spec.md (AC9, AC10, AC13, AC17, AC26, AC27, AC28, AC37, AC47)
Research: Q1 (HEAD /api/hello forwarded, Bun UA), Q2, Q3, Q15 (auth: both; any Authorization scheme is bearer), Q18 (literal anthropic-ratelimit-* on 429/500/529)
Why this approach: the adapter is a value type returning constants; AuthKind checks header keys in the map, never Get, so an empty value still counts as present and no value is read. ErrorBody marshals a two-field struct so the envelope is always valid JSON in the wire field order.
Alternatives rejected: reading the Authorization scheme to tell bearer from others (Q15 says presence only); a literal envelope string built by concatenation (a reason with a quote would break the JSON).
Trade-off / known limit: the tests carry their own copies of core_test's helpers (upstream recorder, raw sender, access-line reader, leak check), since package core_test is not importable.
